## Summary

### Task Completed: Verify display pages work with new tables

Created `e2e/tests/display-pages.spec.ts` with 7 comprehensive tests that verify `gfx.html`, `screen.html`, and `fullscreen.html` work correctly with the new `meeting_participant` system:

1. **gfx.html loads with meeting-scoped JWT** - Verifies the GFX overlay page loads and displays sak title
2. **screen.html loads with meeting-scoped JWT** - Verifies the screen display page works
3. **fullscreen.html loads with meeting-scoped JWT** - Verifies the fullscreen audience display works
4. **gfx.html displays sak title correctly** - Tests specific sak title rendering
5. **screen.html shows content when sak exists** - Tests screen with sak data
6. **fullscreen.html works for audience display** - Tests audience display functionality
7. **display pages work with participant JWT (via invite)** - Critically tests that users who join via invites can access display pages

### Key Technical Details

The display pages use legacy components (`roi-gfx-title`, `roi-gfx-vote`, `roi-gfx-speaker`, `roi-speeches-list`) that rely on:
- `person` table data via `peopleById`, `peopleDelegates`
- `speech` table with `speakerId` referencing `person.id`
- JWT claims containing `person_id`

The previously created migration 019 (`019-participant-person-bridge.sql`) bridges the new and legacy systems by:
- Adding `person_id` column to `meeting_participant`
- Creating a `person` record when users join via invites
- Returning the `person.id` in the meeting-scoped JWT

This ensures complete compatibility - all 7 tests pass!

### Test Results
- 63 tests passed (including 7 new display page tests)
- 2 tests skipped (UI integration tests for /i/ route and QR code)
- 3 tests failed (legacy voting tests - expected, documented as postponed)
